{
  "description": "Generic declarative biology-network renderer — a fixed roster of nodes/edges/shapes (cells and organelles, food-web trophic links, or classification taxa) drawn once on a biology-canvas with no interaction or transitions. Node/edge/shape vocabulary is entirely config-declared, so the same mechanism serves any static biology diagram. Standalone by default; behind a lab router set matchMode and it renders only when MODE_SELECTED matches.",
